axis: attribution-granularity
axis_gloss: "whether each individual claim names its source, or attribution is declared once for a whole document"
poles:
  a: per-claim-attribution
  b: document-level-attribution
split: leaning
draft_status: axis-only
leverage: 7.6
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(9) x split_weight(0.7) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  On attribution granularity — whether each individual claim names its source,
  or attribution is declared once for a whole document — the records assert both
  per claim attribution (7 judgments, 4 authored) and document level attribution
  (2 judgments, 0 authored). Which should be the stated rule, and where is the
  exception?

why_it_matters: >
  Until this is answered, a record below Dave inherits whichever side it happens
  to copy. Full draft pending: the proposal batch for this axis did not
  complete; the axis, poles, counts and evidence are real, the options below are
  the generic form.

